  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing access to life-saving WASH services for internally displaced people living in Areesha and Washokani camps in Northeast Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe proposed intervention aims to provide emergency WASH services for camp populations in Northeast Syria.ltbrgtTo achieve this objective, Acted will provide water trucking as well as water monitoring and chlorination to ensure safe access to water in Areesha camp. Furthermore, Acted will provide essential sanitation services, including desludging, latrine cleaning and WASH facilities maintenance in both Areesha and Washokani camps. Finally, Acted will contribute to environmental health through solid waste management for the individuals residing in Areesha and Washokani camps. ltbrgtThis will benefit a total of 28,852 individuals, namely 12,823 individuals (2,585 households) in Areesha camp and 16,210 individuals (2,256 households) in Washokani camp. This assistance is critical as WASH service provision in the targeted camps has been a gap since the U.S. funding cuts that occurred in early 2025. Camp residents solely rely on humanitarian assistance to meet their WASH basic needs, and received very limited support since then. ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
